      "location": "Definition, final paragraph on recovering the Cauchy boundary term",
      "defect": "unlicensed-inference",
      "evidence": "The paragraph says to apply the interior weak identity to “φ(t,x)ζ(t/δ),” with ζ increasing from 0 to 1 on (0,1). The identity is tested in C_c∞(Π_T), whose test functions must have support compactly contained in the open set. The stated conditions do not require ζ to vanish on a positive interval after 0, so this product need not be an admissible test. A cutoff vanishing near t=0 or an integration over (ε,T) supplies the missing boundary-limit step; the conclusion itself is unaffected.",
